# Launch profile of the speculative configuration (RadixArk DFlash2, K = 7, --max-num-seqs 128). Source it AFTER env/host.env
# and ONLY for speculative launches: it is not part of host.env on purpose (host.env is sourced by every launch, the non-speculative
# --max-num-seqs 256 launch included, whose 384..511-token prefill batches would then move onto the sequence-parallel stream
# without anybody having measured them).
#
# Why: a verify batch has 8 tokens per request. With the default capture list (graphs up to 512 tokens) the verify batches of 33..64
# requests (264..512 tokens) either replay a graph or run on the replicated stream, with the pooler / unpooler GEMMs computed on
# every rank (8x the FLOPs, ~100-120 us per call at 512 rows). The vLLM branch keeps the sequence-parallel (SP) stream off every
# batch the graph dispatcher can serve: the floor is max(MIN_TOKENS, 257, largest capture size + 1), so with graphs up to 512 tokens
# the floor is 513 whatever MIN_TOKENS says (an env value below 513 is silently raised). Capturing graphs only up to 256 tokens and
# lowering the floor to 384 shards the stream from 48 requests (T = 384) on; those batches run eagerly (T > 256).
# S1-9 lever 1 A/B (2 sessions per arm, real prompts, exact KV bytes 9,676,390,400): real 512-token outputs c48 +3.6 %, c64 +5.7 %
# (the SP effect alone +4.3 % / +6.5 %, the eager tax -0.6 % / -0.8 %), 128-token mix rows c48 / c64 +0.4 / +1.4 % greedy,
# c16 / c32 / c128 flat within +-1.3 %. Details: docs/s19_spec_launch.md.
#
# The two settings are ONE launch property and must travel together:
#   - MIN_TOKENS=384 alone changes nothing (floor stays 513): the run is the old configuration;
#   - --max-cudagraph-capture-size 256 alone (env unset) gives the floor max(512, 257, 257) = 512 (A/B arm B512): 257..511-token
#     batches run eagerly and replicated, SP starts at 512 (c64 only), and NVML min free was 340 / 624 MiB against 920 / 772 MiB with
#     floor 384 and 400 / 484 MiB on the default list. Do not use it. Raising the env above the cap (MIN_TOKENS=520, arm B520:
#     257..519 eager and replicated) is the control that reached NVML min free 116 / 30 MiB (no OOM, no margin).
# After every boot run scripts/check_spec_launch.sh <serve.log>: it fails unless the log shows floor 384, graphs up to 256 and the chunk of 8199 tokens (S1-9 L5).
#
# Usage (harness serve_sd.sh; SERVE_EXTRA carries the capture flag and the KV bytes of this profile):
#   source $HOST_DIR/env/host.env; source $HOST_DIR/env/spec_k7.env
#   SERVE_EXTRA="$MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS --kv-cache-memory-bytes $MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES" SPEC_CONFIG=dflash2_radixark ... serve_sd.sh <tag> ...
# or for a plain `vllm serve` line: vllm serve ... --speculative-config '<json>' $MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS --kv-cache-memory-bytes $MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES
#
# S1-9 lever 2 (prefill overlap beside the drafter, r2e): this profile also turns on the microbatched prefill under speculation
# (VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_PREFILL_OVERLAP_SPECULATIVE=1; the vLLM branch keeps it off under speculation otherwise, because it adds a persistent
# ~145 MiB per rank and so moves the exact KV bytes of every speculative launch line). The flag and the KV bytes below are ONE property:
# the bytes of an r2e-on launch are 10,373,877,760 (506,537 blocks = 1,460,755 KV tokens per rank, -1.45 % against the r2e-off 10,526,351,360);
# r2e on with the r2e-off bytes leaves S_live 1,210 MiB (< the 1,256 MiB floor), r2e off with the r2e-on bytes just wastes 145 MiB.
# scripts/check_spec_launch.sh checks the pairing from the boot log and serve_cmd.txt. The other speculative rows of S1-7 (nvidia DFlash2,
# DSpark, mns 64, the default capture list) keep r2e off and their S1-7 bytes: never source this file for them. Details: docs/s19_spec_launch.md.
#
# KV bytes (MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES, below; see the S1-13 / S1-9 L7 paragraph further down for the current value: the flag-2 bytes of the 0.33.0 line): the exact --kv-cache-memory-bytes of this configuration, re-derived with the S1-7 procedure for this graph set. The graph pool
# shrinks from 2.11 to 1.22 GiB per rank (idle memory -912 MiB), so the S1-7 value 9,676,390,400 of the default capture list leaves S_live 2,167 MiB here (floor 1,256 MiB);
# 10,526,351,360 (513,982 blocks = 1,482,225 KV tokens, +8.8 %) leaves S_live 1,356.6 MiB with r2e off (lever 1 only), clean over the S1-7 stress (REPS = 2) and the GSM8K / determinism gates.
# With r2e on (this file, lever 2): 10,373,877,760 (506,537 blocks = 1,460,755 KV tokens, -1.45 % against the r2e-off value) leaves S_live 1,354.4 MiB over the S1-7 stress extended by the
# prefix-hit and split / unsplit phases (H, I), clean, and passes the GSM8K / determinism gates of lever 2.
# Valid without prompt_logprobs / echo (S1-7 section 4). It belongs to this profile only: with the default capture list use 9,676,390,400. Re-derive it after any change
# of the sampler, the verify path, the graph set or max-num-batched-tokens (S1-7). The NVML min free of a boot is not the gate (it varies with the allocator cache).
#
# S1-9 L4 (the DFlash2 aux projection on each rank's rows, VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FC_SHARD=2, the vLLM default since the L4 merge; exported below so the profile does not
# depend on the tree's default): the target's forward runs the draft's aux fc on each rank's T / 8 rows under SP (one [T / 8, 8192] gather instead of 5 tap gathers + a full-chunk fc)
# and as a rank slice + gather inside the FULL decode graph below the SP floor. The S1-7 stress of this profile (REPS = 2, A1 B C1 C2 D H I L X) measured idle +270 MiB free and
# a live growth of 1,813 MiB (2,269 before: the prefill transient shrinks), so S_live at 10,373,877,760 is 2,080 MiB; the bytes of this profile are therefore
# 11,134,914,560 (543,697 blocks = 1,567,918 KV tokens per rank, +107,163 tokens = +7.3 %, 11.96x "maximum concurrency for 131,072 tokens per request"), S_live 1,354.2 MiB
# (floor 1,256), clean over the same stress. THE FLAG AND THE BYTES ARE ONE PROPERTY: with the flag at 0 (or on an older tree, or when it falls back) the larger value leaves S_live
# of ~630 MiB. MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES below is therefore set from the flag: 11,134,914,560 when the flag is 2 (the file default of the S1-9 L4 state; the current default is the FP8 draft value of the S1-13 / S1-9 L7 paragraph below), else the previous 10,373,877,760;
# scripts/check_spec_launch.sh checks the pairing from the boot log ("the aux projection runs in the target's forward") and serve_cmd.txt.
#
# A preset value is kept (":=", as host.env does), e.g. VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_MIN_TOKENS=520 plus the capture flag
# is the eager, replicated control of the A/B; scripts/check_spec_launch.sh takes the expected floor as its second argument.
: "${VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_MIN_TOKENS:=384}"
export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_MIN_TOKENS
# S1-9 L5 (B3, aligned prefill chunks): under K = 7 the default budget of 8192 gives 8185-token chunks (8192 - 7; measured, S1-9 L2: one
# sp_reduce_scatter F.pad staging copy per layer and a 7-token tail step for an 8192-token prompt). --max-num-batched-tokens 8199 gives 8192-row chunks: A/B of the S1-9 L5 hold (2^3 factorial,
# 4 boots per level, TTFT medians of single random-id requests) -3.54 % at 16,384 tokens, -2.69 % at 32,768, -4.31 % at 8,192 (the aligned single chunk), natural 8192-token prompts c1 +2.4 %, c16 -0.9 %,
# c64 -0.5 %, mixed churn +0.3 %, decode cells within +-0.7 % (greedy c1 .. c128, default c1 .. c128), no acceptance-length trip. The KV bytes stay 11,134,914,560 (S1-7 stress REPS = 2: S_live
# 1,278.4 MiB, floor 1,256; 1,567,538 KV tokens per rank with the flag, 1,567,918 without it: the sliding-window groups reserve per scheduled token). MUSE_SPEC_MNBT overrides the value
# (8192 = the old chunks); scripts/check_spec_launch.sh checks the log line and serve_cmd.txt (SPEC_EXPECT_MNBT).
: "${MUSE_SPEC_MNBT:=8199}"
# S1-14 F2 (cap the scheduled tokens at 8192): on the vLLM 0.33.0 line the DFlash drafter takes no slots in the target batch
# (SpeculativeConfig.max_num_new_slots_for_drafting is 0, it was K = 7 on 0.32.0), so a prefill chunk is min(max_num_scheduled_tokens,
# max_num_batched_tokens - 0) = 8199 tokens and the S1-9 L5 alignment is lost (8199 % 8 = 7: the r2e microbatches of 4100 / 4099 rows take the
# sp_reduce_scatter F.pad staging copies again and other cuBLAS tiles; 32k cold prefill +2.0 % client wall against 0.32.0). The flag
# --max-num-scheduled-tokens 8192 caps the scheduler's per-step budget (vllm/config/scheduler.py:55, vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py:139-141,
# :719-722) and gives 8192-row chunks again; max_num_batched_tokens stays 8199, which is what sizes the runner buffers, the profile run, the
# cudagraph range, the SP / MoE engine buffers and the sliding-window KV reservation (gpu_model_runner.py:524, config/vllm.py:611-620,
# :2569), so the memory profile and the KV pool are expected not to move (to be verified in the S1-14 boots: KV blocks per rank, READY MiB): THE KV BYTES BELOW ARE EXPECTED TO STAY
# (11,720,212,480 for the flag-2 profile) and flag and bytes travel together. MUSE_SPEC_MNST overrides the value (0 = no flag: the 8199-token
# chunks of the plain 0.33.0 port; a mixed step loses 7 tokens of budget with the flag). scripts/check_spec_launch.sh checks the "non-default
# args" log line and serve_cmd.txt (SPEC_EXPECT_MNST).
: "${MUSE_SPEC_MNST:=8192}"
case "$MUSE_SPEC_MNST" in
  off) MUSE_SPEC_MNST=0 ;;
  ""|*[!0-9]*) echo "spec_k7.env: MUSE_SPEC_MNST must be a number or 0 (off), got '$MUSE_SPEC_MNST'" >&2; return 1 2>/dev/null || exit 1 ;;
esac
if [ "$MUSE_SPEC_MNST" -gt "$MUSE_SPEC_MNBT" ] 2>/dev/null; then
  echo "spec_k7.env: MUSE_SPEC_MNST $MUSE_SPEC_MNST exceeds MUSE_SPEC_MNBT $MUSE_SPEC_MNBT (the cap would grow the b12x warmup and capacity to max(MNBT, cap))" >&2; return 1 2>/dev/null || exit 1
fi
# S1-9 L11 (sequence parallel inside the FULL decode graphs, A1a, ON by default since the L11 gate; A1b, the capture list to 384, is NOT adopted):
#   MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_SP_MIN_TOKENS=<n> (default 136; 0 = off): exports VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_GRAPH_MIN_TOKENS=<n>: the warm-up / capture pass of a decode-only FULL graph shards every verify batch of at least n tokens
#     (raised to the decode MoE engine's limit + 1 = 129); eager, mixed and PIECEWISE batches keep the floor of this profile. 136 shards the verify batches of 17..32 requests in the graphs the profile captures anyway (graphs <= 256, pool 0.92 GiB
#     against 0.95: no KV cost, the bytes below are unchanged and leave S_live 1,302.5 MiB (production 1,278.5), floor 1,256). Gate (4 boot groups, real prompts, STEADY, guards, determinism, GSM8K): docs/s19_spec_launch.md "S1-9 L11".
#     THE FLAG NEEDS A vLLM TREE WITH THE FEATURE (branch 6da60b3062 + the L11 commits): scripts/check_spec_launch.sh FAILS a launch whose boot logs no graph-floor line, no flagged FULL decode graph at or above the floor, or another floor.
#   MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_CAP=<tokens> (default 256): the largest capture size of --max-cudagraph-capture-size. A cap above 256 (384 / 400 / 512: the default grid adds steps of 16, 272 .. cap) puts the verify batches of 33 .. cap/8 requests into FULL graphs
#     too (A1b) and costs graph pool: NOT ADOPTED (the L11 gate: STEADY c33..c47 -10..-15 % step, but real prompts only +2.55 % at c36..c48 against 1.96 % of the KV tokens lost, and the TTFT of 256 / 257-token prompts next to 16 / 8 decoders (mixed steps of T = 384, the edge where a cap-384 list turns
#     eager SP into a replicated PIECEWISE graph, and 321) 6.5 .. 7.5 % worse). Exact bytes of cap 384 with the graph floor: 11,346,923,520 (554,049 blocks, 1,597,384 KV tokens per rank, S_live 1,278.5 MiB; 0.32.0-derived, not re-derived on 0.33.0; safe because 0.33.0 leaves more room at equal bytes); MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES_OVERRIDE=<bytes> must carry the bytes of any other cap and
#     scripts/check_spec_launch.sh FAILS a cap above 256 that is not checked against SPEC_CAP_MAX_BYTES=<bytes>. The eager floor becomes cap + 1 (max(MIN_TOKENS, 257, cap + 1)): mixed batches of 257 .. cap tokens run in PIECEWISE graphs, replicated.
#   The pairing check: scripts/check_spec_launch.sh <serve.log> [floor [cap]] (defaults: the floor and cap of the sourcing shell) with SPEC_EXPECT_GRAPH_SP=off|<n> (graph floor line of the boot log). Details: docs/s19_spec_launch.md "S1-9 L11".
: "${MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_SP_MIN_TOKENS:=136}"
: "${MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_CAP:=256}"
if [ "$MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_SP_MIN_TOKENS" != 0 ]; then
  VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_GRAPH_MIN_TOKENS=$MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_SP_MIN_TOKENS
  export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_GRAPH_MIN_TOKENS
else
  # off is a property of sourcing this profile: a value exported by an earlier source of it (or by hand) does not survive
  unset VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_GRAPH_MIN_TOKENS
fi
MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS="--max-cudagraph-capture-size $MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_CAP --max-num-batched-tokens $MUSE_SPEC_MNBT"
if [ "$MUSE_SPEC_MNST" != 0 ]; then
  MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS="$MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS --max-num-scheduled-tokens $MUSE_SPEC_MNST"
fi
export MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS
VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_PREFILL_OVERLAP_SPECULATIVE=1
export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_PREFILL_OVERLAP_SPECULATIVE
: "${VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FC_SHARD:=2}"
export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FC_SHARD
# S1-9 L7 (the DFlash2 draft in FP8, VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FP8, kernel cutlass): the draft's linear layers and its candidate head run in FP8 (e4m3 weights, one scale per output channel, cutlass W8A8) since S1-9 L7: STEADY step -3.2 % at c1, pooled real-prompt c1 / c16 / c32 tok/s +1.50 % (SIG), acceptance length unchanged (draft-weighted dAL -0.010), +3.94 % KV tokens; flag 0 restores the bf16 draft. Details: docs/s19_spec_launch.md.
# THE FLAG, THE KERNEL AND THE BYTES ARE ONE PROPERTY: the idle memory at identical bytes differs per (flag, kernel) (cutlass 2: -418 MiB, cutlass 1: -616, marlin 2: -542, marlin 1: -740 against the bf16 draft; the
# hook's "670 MiB freed" is numel arithmetic, not the allocator delta), and production S_live sits ~22 MiB above the 1,256 MiB floor, so the bytes are derived per state with the S1-7 procedure:
# flag 2 (layers + FP8 candidate head, cutlass): 11,720,212,480 (572,276 blocks = 1,649,935 KV tokens per rank, S_live 1,278.4 MiB, REPS = 2 stress A1 B C1 C2 D H I L M X), re-derived on the vLLM 0.33.0 line (S1-13, 2026-11-10; the 0.32.0 value was 11,573,411,840 = 565,108 blocks = 1,629,269 tokens). The other values below are 0.32.0-derived (S1-9 L4 / L7 / L2, not re-derived on 0.33.0, kept unchanged): flag 1 (layers only, cutlass): 11,781,017,600 (575,245 blocks = 1,658,495 tokens, S_live 1,278.4 MiB on 0.32.0); flag 0 (bf16 draft): 11,134,914,560; FC_SHARD != 2: 10,373,877,760. A Marlin launch keeps the bytes of the same flag with cutlass (Marlin leaves ~124 MiB
# more room: safe, not derived). scripts/check_spec_launch.sh reads the state from the success lines "DFlash2 draft weights in FP8 (...=<n>, kernel <k>): 30 linear layers quantized" / "DFlash2 candidate head in FP8" and fails a
# boot that carries more than the maximum of its state, a flag set without the success line, or a "does not apply" warning (a silent fall back to bf16 or to flag 1).
: "${VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FP8:=2}"
export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FP8
: "${VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FP8_KERNEL:=cutlass}"
export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FP8_KERNEL
if [ "$VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FC_SHARD" = 2 ]; then
  case "$VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_DRAFT_FP8" in
    2) MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES=11720212480 ;;   # S1-13: derived on the vLLM 0.33.0 line (572,276 blocks, 1,649,935 KV tokens per rank)
    1) MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES=11781017600 ;;   # 0.32.0-derived (S1-9 L7), not re-derived on 0.33.0
    *) MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES=11134914560 ;;   # flag 0: the L4 / L5 bytes (a bf16 draft), 0.32.0-derived
  esac
else
  MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES=10373877760   # 0.32.0-derived (not re-derived on 0.33.0): the r2e-on bytes derived without the aux projection on the target's rows (S1-9 L2); an FP8 draft there is not derived: the same (safe) bytes
fi
# S1-9 L11: the exact bytes of a launch with another capture list (cap > 256: a larger graph pool) come from the S1-7 procedure and are passed in; without an override the bytes above are the cap-256 ones.
if [ -n "${MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES_OVERRIDE:-}" ]; then
  MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES=$MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES_OVERRIDE
elif [ "$MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_CAP" -gt 256 ]; then
  echo "env/spec_k7.env: MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_CAP=$MUSE_SPEC_GRAPH_CAP > 256 with the bytes of the cap-256 pool ($MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES): not derived (set MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES_OVERRIDE, check_spec_launch.sh needs SPEC_CAP_MAX_BYTES)" >&2
fi
export MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES
